Error: Jet.CopyNotSupported: `Lease` can't be copied out of the place it is read from
  --> Tests/UI/resource_taken_receiver_in_place.jet:18:56
    |
 18 | element_field: fn(packages: &&[Package]) { packages[0].lease.release() }
    |                                                        ^^^^^
 Why: It holds a resource, which has one cleanup owner; this position takes an owned value, so the copy and the place would both close the same resource
 Fix: Use the element where it is, or remove it from its collection to own it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.CopyNotSupported

Error: Jet.CopyNotSupported: `Lease` can't be copied out of the place it is read from
  --> Tests/UI/resource_taken_receiver_in_place.jet:23:36
    |
 23 |     read_receiver: fn(self) { self.lease.release() }
    |                                    ^^^^^
 Why: It holds a resource, which has one cleanup owner; this position takes an owned value, so the copy and the place would both close the same resource
 Fix: Use it where it is, or take `self` as a `&&` parameter or receiver and move the field out with `.move()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.CopyNotSupported
